      "math_academy_id": "e-5542",
      "problem": "An inner product on $V = \\mathbb{R}^3$ is given by $\\langle \\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{y} \\rangle =  3 x_1 y_1 + x_2 y_2 + 7 x_3 y_3.$ Find $\\langle \\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{y} \\rangle,$ if\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14149067/assets/c92e466baabcfc0a353b49000e745116a79ec8a85ad7f7c20daaaf526ec37953.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "Computing the inner product according to the definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y⟩ & =3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+7{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1\\cdot (-3)+(-2)\\cdot 1+7\\cdot 0\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-9-2+0 \\\\  & =-11.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
